WEBVTT

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:15.830
Fungus? Fungus? You like cars?

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:20.710
I got a really nice car. If you
let me go, I'll give you a ride

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:23.190
in the car.
Please, Fungus.

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:26.310
I'm sorry, Wazowski,
but Randall said I'm not allowed

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:28.790
to fraternize with victims
of his evil plot.

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:43.710
What happened?
Where's Wazowski?

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:48.910
Where is he?

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:50.550
(WHIMPERING)

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:57.390
-SULLEY: Come on.
-This is crazy. He's gonna kill us.

00:00:57.470 --> 00:00:59.190
CDA AGENT:
That could be contaminated.

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:01.190
We gotta get out of here now!

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:04.870
We could start a new life far away.
Goodbye, Monsters, Inc.

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:06.950
Goodbye, Mr. Waternoose.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:09.510
-No, Mike, wait.
-Hey, what are you doing?

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:13.710
-Follow me. I have an idea.
-No, no, no, no, no.

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:15.510
COMPUTER VOICE:
Simulation terminated.

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:17.550
WATERNOOSE: No, no, no, no, no.

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:21.470
What was that? You're trying
to scare the kid, not lull it to sleep.

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:24.550
I was going for a snake/ninja approach

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:26.070
with a little hissing.

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:27.470
(HISSES)

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:31.350
How many times do I have to tell you?
It's all about presence.

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:34.510
-About how you enter the room.
-Mr. Waternoose!

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:36.710
James, perfect timing.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.710
No, no, sir. You don't understand.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:41.430
-Show these monsters how it's done.
-I can't.

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:44.190
-Sir, you have to listen to me.
-Pay attention.

00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:46.710
You're about to see
the best in the business.

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:49.550
-Reset the simulator.
-But sir!

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:51.510
MOTHER: Good night, sweetheart.
ANIMATRONIC BOY: 'Night, Mom.

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:53.590
-Kitty!
-No, Boo, no!

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:57.310
-Give us a big loud roar.
-There's no time for this!

00:01:57.390 --> 00:02:00.150
-What are you waiting for? Roar.
-But, sir...

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:01.750
Roar!

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:03.590
(ROARING FEROCIOUSLY)

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:05.030
(SHRIEKING IN TERROR)

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:11.470
(BOO CRYING)

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:12.590
(STUDENTS APPLAUDING)

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:15.390
Well done. Well done, James.

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:17.110
-Boo?
-All right, gentlemen.

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:20.470
-Right this way.
-I hope you've learned a lesson today.

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:24.230
(FEARFUL WHIMPER)

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:26.190
Boo.

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:31.830
Boo.

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:38.790
Boo, it's me.

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:43.950
-(GASPS) The child!
-Sir, she isn't toxic.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:46.630
-It sounds crazy, but trust me.
-Boo?

00:02:47.110 --> 00:02:48.630
No, no, no, no, it's OK.

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:50.590
I was just... No.

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:54.710
No, don't be scared.
That wasn't real.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:57.670
It's just a... I was just...

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:14.710
-Boo.
-MIKE: ...test it out on that sweet girl.

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:17.830
-Boo.
-...have her, he is trying to kill us.

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:20.030
-This is Randall's fault.
-Randall?

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:23.350
We can take you to his secret lab
in this factory.

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:27.550
How could this happen?
How could this happen?

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:30.750
Does anyone else know about this?

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:32.230
-No, sir.
-Good.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:35.350
This company can't afford
any more bad publicity.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:38.710
Now, before we do anything else,

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:41.910
let's take care of the child.

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:48.630
I never thought
things would come to this.

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:50.710
Not in my factory.

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:55.190
I'm sorry you boys got mixed up in this.

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:56.750
Especially you, James.

00:03:57.190 --> 00:04:00.190
But now we can
set everything straight again.

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:01.870
For the good of the company.

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:08.190
Sir? That's not her door.

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:09.870
I know, I know.

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:14.230
It's yours.

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:15.430
(GASPS)

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:17.510
(BOTH SCREAMING)

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:20.230
No!

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:24.550
Boo!

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:34.390
No! No! No, no, no, no!

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:38.510
It's too late.
We're banished, genius!

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:40.230
We're in the human world.

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:43.870
What a great idea,
going to your old pal Waternoose.

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:46.030
Too bad he was in on the whole thing.

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:48.750
All you had to do was listen to me.

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:52.950
Just once!
But you didn't, did you?

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:55.430
You're still not listening!

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:03.670
Take that!

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:04.870
(BOTH SNARLING)

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:05.910
(GASPS)

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:11.590
Welcome to the Himalayas.

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:18.030
Abominable. Can you believe that?

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:19.950
Do I look abominable to you?

00:05:20.110 --> 00:05:22.310
Why can't they call me
the Adorable Snowman

00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:25.430
or the Agreeable Snowman,
for crying out loud?

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:28.270
I'm a nice guy.
Snow cone?

00:05:29.230 --> 00:05:31.910
No, don't worry. It's lemon.

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:35.390
How about you, big fella?
Snow cone?

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:40.790
Did you see the way she looked at me?

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:47.430
Poor guy. I understand.
It ain't easy being banished.

00:05:47.710 --> 00:05:49.150
Take my buddy, Bigfoot.

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:53.470
When he was banished, he fashioned
an enormous diaper out of poison ivy.

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:55.550
Wore it on his head like a tiara.

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:59.470
Called himself King Itchy.
It won't be so hard for you guys.

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:01.030
How lucky can you get?

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:04.470
-Banished with your best friend.
-He is not my friend.

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:08.550
I just assumed you were buddies.
When I saw you in the snow hugging...

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:11.630
Look at that big jerk.
Ruined my life. And for what?

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:12.750
A stupid kid!

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:16.310
Because of you I am now stuck
in this frozen wasteland.

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:19.710
Wasteland?
I think you mean wonderland.

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:22.230
How about all this fabulous snow?

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:24.950
And wait till you see
the local village.

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:29.030
Cutest thing in the world.
I haven't mentioned the free yaks' milk.

00:06:29.670 --> 00:06:31.670
-What did you say?
-Yaks' milk.

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:33.830
Milking a yak ain't exactly a picnic.

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:36.350
Once you pick the hairs out
it's nutritious.

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:38.870
No, about a village.
Are there kids in it?

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:42.190
Kids? Sure. Tough kids, sissy kids,
kids who climb on rocks.

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:44.750
-Where is it?
-At the bottom of the mountain.

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:47.630
-A three-day hike.
-Three days?

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:49.710
We need to get there now.

